<title>USA: Synalloy sees oper income rise.</title>
<headline>Synalloy sees oper income rise.</headline>
<dateline>SPARTANBURG, S.C. 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Synalloy Corp said on Friday that it expects improvement in quarterly operating income on a sequential basis to begin in the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>The company said that the sales decline in 1996 resulted from lower prices since unit volume was up slightly.</p>
<p>The decline in operating income was caused by weaker market conditions and inventory losses from declining prices, the company said.</p>
<p>-- ((New York newsdesk 212-859-1611))</p>
